  planner_response {
    response: "I have redesigned and updated the Smart Travel Itinerary Planner to create an accessible, non-technical, and senior-friendly experience:\n\n### 1. Currency Standardization to INR (\342\202\271)\n- **All Budgets & Estimates**: Converted all budget selections, monument admissions, daily meals, hotel tariffs per night, and dining for two into Indian Rupees (**\342\202\271 / INR**).\n- **Preset Tiers**: Pocket-Friendly (\342\202\2711,500 \342\200\223 \342\202\2713,500/day), Comfort / Standard (\342\202\2714,000 \342\200\223 \342\202\2719,000/day), and Premium / Luxury (\342\202\27110,000 \342\200\223 \342\202\27125,000+/day).\n\n### 2. Simplified, Calming & Accessible UI\n- **Warm & Readable Visual Design**: Replaced dense, intimidating layouts with a calming off-white warm canvas, generous line spacing, high color contrast, and clear typography.\n- **Senior-Friendly Text Size Toggle**: Added a one-click **\"Larger Text (A+)\"** toggle in the header for easy reading.\n- **Dedicated Accessibility Preferences**: Included options for relaxed pacing, minimal stairs & elevator-accessible attractions, pure vegetarian dining, and AC transit.\n\n### 3. Removed Technical Clutter & Added PDF Print\n- **No JSON / Markdown Noise**: Removed JSON schema modals and Markdown code export buttons.\n- **One-Click Print / Save PDF**: Added a prominent **\"Print / Save PDF\"** action with customized print styling to easily generate clean, printable physical travel schedules.\n\n### 4. Researched Photography\n- **Context-Aware Imagery**: Integrated researched, high-definition photography for destinations, landmarks, palaces, hotels, and authentic local cuisines.\n\n### 5. Dedicated Sections & Tabs\n- \360\237\217\250 **Hotels & Stays**: Dedicated recommendations across budget tiers with price per night in \342\202\271, neighborhood proximity, and accessibility highlights.\n- \360\237\215\275\357\270\217 **Food & Dining Guide**: Dedicated dining guide with signature dishes, pure vegetarian ratings, approx cost for two in \342\202\271, and comfort dining tips.\n- \360\237\227\243\357\270\217 **Local Dialect & Survival Phrasebook**: Common phrases categorized by water/food safety, directions, polite bargaining, and emergency help with phonetic English pronunciations.\n- \342\234\250 **Fascinating Fun Facts & Trivia**: Researched historical and cultural trivia at the conclusion of the itinerary."
    thinking: "**Verifying Currency Implementation**\n\nI\'ve just finished auditing all the components to ensure INR is consistently used. Specifically, I\'ve checked and confirmed that the backend prompts, data schemas, sample datasets, budget selectors, cost figures, hotel tariffs, restaurant prices, and admissions are all rendered in Indian Rupees (\342\202\271).\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have redesigned and updated the Smart Travel Itinerary Planner to create an accessible, non-technical, and senior-friendly experience:\n\n### 1. Currency Standardization to INR (\342\202\271)\n- **All Budgets & Estimates**: Converted all budget selections, monument admissions, daily meals, hotel tariffs per night, and dining for two into Indian Rupees (**\342\202\271 / INR**).\n- **Preset Tiers**: Pocket-Friendly (\342\202\2711,500 \342\200\223 \342\202\2713,500/day), Comfort / Standard (\342\202\2714,000 \342\200\223 \342\202\2719,000/day), and Premium / Luxury (\342\202\27110,000 \342\200\223 \342\202\27125,000+/day).\n\n### 2. Simplified, Calming & Accessible UI\n- **Warm & Readable Visual Design**: Replaced dense, intimidating layouts with a calming off-white warm canvas, generous line spacing, high color contrast, and clear typography.\n- **Senior-Friendly Text Size Toggle**: Added a one-click **\"Larger Text (A+)\"** toggle in the header for easy reading.\n- **Dedicated Accessibility Preferences**: Included options for relaxed pacing, minimal stairs & elevator-accessible attractions, pure vegetarian dining, and AC transit.\n\n### 3. Removed Technical Clutter & Added PDF Print\n- **No JSON / Markdown Noise**: Removed JSON schema modals and Markdown code export buttons.\n- **One-Click Print / Save PDF**: Added a prominent **\"Print / Save PDF\"** action with customized print styling to easily generate clean, printable physical travel schedules.\n\n### 4. Researched Photography\n- **Context-Aware Imagery**: Integrated researched, high-definition photography for destinations, landmarks, palaces, hotels, and authentic local cuisines.\n\n### 5. Dedicated Sections & Tabs\n- \360\237\217\250 **Hotels & Stays**: Dedicated recommendations across budget tiers with price per night in \342\202\271, neighborhood proximity, and accessibility highlights.\n- \360\237\215\275\357\270\217 **Food & Dining Guide**: Dedicated dining guide with signature dishes, pure vegetarian ratings, approx cost for two in \342\202\271, and comfort dining tips.\n- \360\237\227\243\357\270\217 **Local Dialect & Survival Phrasebook**: Common phrases categorized by water/food safety, directions, polite bargaining, and emergency help with phonetic English pronunciations.\n- \342\234\250 **Fascinating Fun Facts & Trivia**: Researched historical and cultural trivia at the conclusion of the itinerary."
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 585408104
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
