  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Code Integration**\n\nI\'m currently focused on integrating Leaflet\'s CSS into the project, contemplating the best place to import it\342\200\224either `src/main.tsx` or `src/index.css`. Following that, I\'m working on a design refresh of updates to `src/types.ts`. I\'m starting by adding coordinate properties to the various data structures; `ActivityItem`, `DayItinerary`, `HotelRecommendation`, and `Restaurant` will all get coordinates.\n\n\n**Expanding Trip Data Structures**\n\nI\'m now diving into augmenting the data structures, specifically `TripSummary`, to include `destination_coords`, and rolling out currency support with associated symbols. I\'m also adding `flight_info` to provide flight route recommendations and airport details. Further, I\'m working to introduce a `saved_trips` type for itinerary management and to add expanded types for hotels and restaurants with filters and tags. Finally, I\'m working on substantially expanding landmark and city image mappings with curated high-resolution photos for many destinations across Europe and Asia.\n\n\n**Adding Global Data Categories**\n\nI\'m now expanding the data categories. I\'m focusing on high-fidelity food photos for specific categories like ramen and street tacos. I\'m also adding hotel aesthetics, such as \"grand heritage palace\" and \"modern luxury high-rise.\" This data should enhance the application\'s visual appeal.\n\n\n**Developing Map Functionality**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating flight details with suggestions for airports and route recommendations. I\'m also preparing for the new `InteractiveMapWidget.tsx` component, which will be Bento-styled with Leaflet/OpenStreetMap. Key features I\'m aiming for are day and category filters, numbered pins for activities, custom popup cards, and a route polyline.\n\n\n**Implementing Route Display**\n\nI\'m now focused on the interactive map. I\'m adding connectors to show travel paths between activities for each day and buttons to open routes in Google Maps and export to Google My Maps. I\'m also including a fullscreen toggle and fit-to-bounds functionality. Finally, I\'m working to integrate a flight finder section with origin airport selectors and direct search buttons to other platforms.\n\n\n**Organizing Trip Saving Features**\n\nI\'m now implementing the ability to save the current trip with a custom name or timestamp. I\'m also working on listing saved trips, and the display will include a thumbnail, destination, days, budget, and date saved. I am adding one-click options to load, export as JSON, export as KML for Google My Maps, download as .ics for Google Calendar, or delete.\n\n**Integrating Navbar Enhancements**\n\nI\'ve just added a global currency selector dropdown to the `Navbar.tsx` component, including USD, EUR, GBP, INR, JPY, AUD, CAD, AED, and SGD. I\'ve also integrated a \"Saved Trips\" button with a badge indicating the saved trip count, and a \"Save Plan\" button for immediate itinerary bookmarking. Additionally, there are quick actions to access Google Maps and export options, as well as a \"Larger Font (A+)\" accessibility toggle.\n\n**Refining Planner and Itinerary**\n\nI\'m updating `PlannerForm.tsx` to include a currency selector directly in the budget step and global destination suggestions. I\'ve added an origin city input for flight estimations. Meanwhile, in `ItineraryView.tsx`, I\'ve added tabs for Day-by-Day Plan, Interactive Map with Google Maps export, and a Flights & Route tab.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 678344843
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
