  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing User Requests**\n\nI\'m currently focused on dissecting the initial user requests, specifically targeting the directive to \"remove emojis.\" I\'m systematically examining several files \342\200\223 `sampleData.ts`, `TripSummaryHeader.tsx`, `DayScheduleCard.tsx`, `HotelSection.tsx`, `RestaurantSection.tsx`, `FlightFinderSection.tsx`, `SurvivalPhrasesSection.tsx`, `FunFactsSection.tsx`, `CostBreakdownCard.tsx`, and `Logistics` \342\200\223 to pinpoint all emoji occurrences. This comprehensive scan is a necessary first step.\n\n\n**Expanding Emoji Removal Scope**\n\nI\'ve broadened the emoji removal scope to include several new files: `GuideCard.tsx`, `InteractiveMapWidget.tsx`, `PlannerForm.tsx`, `Navbar.tsx`, `ItineraryView.tsx`, `SavedTripsModal.tsx`, `ActivitySwapModal.tsx`, and `server.ts`. I am aiming to systematically replace emojis, such as `\342\234\250`, `\342\234\210\357\270\217`, `\360\237\223\215`, etc., with corresponding Lucide icons or text badges. I am also currently working to implement the bar switching bar right after the website\'s main header.\n\n\n**Implementing Direct Import Links**\n\nI\'m now focusing on eliminating download options for `.kml` and `.ics` files. My primary goal is to integrate direct import links. For Google Maps, I\'m working on generating dynamic URLs, including directions and search URLs using waypoints, as well as direct links to Google My Maps.  Furthermore, I\'ll be creating a simple \"Open in Google Maps\" feature to open all location markers. For Google Calendar, I\'m generating a direct import link to streamline the process.\n\n\n**Adding Calendar Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating a quick modal/dropdown for effortless \"Add Trip to Google Calendar\" functionality. I\'m focusing on enabling one-click adding of either the full trip or individual day schedules directly to Google Calendar, eliminating the need for any file downloads.\n\nI\'m also working on implementing a \"Season Adjustment Engine\". I plan to add `start_date` to `PlannerInputs` with an interactive date picker. Then, I will focus on computing the exact calendar date for each day and automatically determining the season based on the selected month and destination latitude/hemisphere. I will then have to display a \"Seasonal Weather & Travel Advisory Banner\" in the Itinerary.\n\n\n**Refining Seasonality & Imagery**\n\nI\'m now focusing on further refining the season-specific information, specifically integrating it into `server.ts` to guide AI responses about travel considerations. I\'m also ensuring the itinerary view toolbar allows for dynamic date changes, instantly updating all day dates and season-related tips. I\'ve also implemented changes to improve image accuracy. I will keep the verified hero image for the destination city in `TripSummaryHeader.tsx` and have removed individual photo thumbnail boxes/images for activities, hotels, and restaurants, replacing them with modern category icons.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 957545050
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
