    thinking: "**Exploring Import Utilities**\n\nI\'m currently focused on enabling direct import and linking capabilities to Google Maps and Calendar within `src/utils/mapExportUtils.ts`. Specifically, I\'m developing functions like `generateAllTripGoogleMapsUrl(plan: ItineraryPlanResponse)` to generate Google Maps URLs and also `generateGoogleCalendar` functions, for integration and exporting.\n\n\n**Developing Event Integration**\n\nI\'ve made considerable progress on creating Google Calendar event URLs, particularly with `EventUrl()`. It generates pre-filled links for the web interface, streamlining calendar event creation. I\'ve also built `generateGoogleCalendarDayUrl()` to incorporate daily schedules and tips. Plus, I\'m working on `openGoogleMyMapsImport()`, facilitating direct import with My Maps using copyable place lists. I\'m moving on to seasonal date analyses and working on the seasonal utility file.\n\n\n**Defining Seasonal Frameworks**\n\nI\'m now diving into season detection logic, considering month and destination. I\'m building a system to categorize the time of year (Spring, Summer, Autumn/Fall, Winter, Monsoon/Dry). This includes handling variations between the Northern and Southern Hemispheres, and Tropical/South Asian regions, incorporating specific climate characteristics for accurate season mapping.\n\n\n"
