    thinking: "**Analyzing Data Sources**\n\nI\'m now carefully examining the sample data within `src/sampleData.ts`, scrutinizing it for any emoji presence in the strings, paying close attention to the Kyoto, Jaipur, Paris, Dubai, and Rome entries. This meticulous check is the main focus, ensuring clean data. Then I\'ll check user requests.\n\n\n**Eliminating Emojis**\n\nI\'m now methodically targeting emoji removal across multiple components: `Navbar.tsx`, `PlannerForm.tsx`, `ItineraryView.tsx`, `TripSummaryHeader.tsx`, `DayScheduleCard.tsx`, `HotelSection.tsx`, `RestaurantSection.tsx`, `FlightFinderSection.tsx`, `SurvivalPhrasesSection.tsx`, `FunFactsSection.tsx`, `CostBreakdownCard.tsx`, `LogisticsGuideCard.tsx`, `SavedTripsModal.tsx`, `ActivitySwapModal.tsx`, and `InteractiveMapWidget.tsx`. I\'ll replace any indicator emojis with Lucide badges where appropriate.\nI\'m ensuring there are no remaining emojis. I am ensuring that the website does not have any emojis in it.\n\nI\'m also maintaining the pages switching bar directly after the main website header.\n\n\n**Integrating New Features**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating new features within `ItineraryView`. I\'ll position the tab bar (Day-by-Day, Map, Flights, etc.) at the very top, and include the Quick Actions (Trip Date, Season, Google Maps import, Calendar, Print, Save) directly below or beside it. Next, I\'ll move on to the Google Maps and Calendar import features.\n\nI\'m replacing `.kml` and `.ics` downloads with direct Google Maps and Calendar integrations. I\'m implementing \"Open in Google Maps\" buttons for both the overall trip and individual locations. Also, I\'m creating a Google Calendar web event URL with pre-filled details. I\'ll add the \"Add to Google Calendar\" feature for both overall trips and individual days.\n\nI\'m integrating a date picker and season selector into `PlannerForm.tsx` to allow date adjustments based on the selected season.\n\n\n**Implementing Date Features**\n\nI\'m now implementing the dynamic Date & Season Bar in `ItineraryView.tsx`, aiming for immediate recalculation of dates based on user input. I\'m focusing on the date input for the start date and the corresponding season detection. The system will display the exact date for each day and present seasonal climate info, including temperature ranges, clothing advice, and attraction recommendations, all based on the season detected. Additionally, I\'m integrating the `start_date` and seasonal instructions into the prompt within `server.ts` to enrich the results.\n\n\n**Refining Component Cards**\n\nI\'m now overhauling the Hotel and Restaurant sections. I\'m removing the photos from both and replacing them with modern Bento-style cards. The Hotel cards will showcase category badges, neighborhood tags, price per night, key highlights, and Google Maps/Booking buttons. Restaurant cards will feature cuisine badges, neighborhood tags, dietary indicators, \"must-try\" dish highlights, cost estimates, and a Google Maps button.\n\nI\'m also keeping the dark mode features. I\'m adding a dark mode toggle to the Navbar and storing the user preference in local storage. I\'m ensuring all the components adapt to dark mode and light mode.\n\n\n"
