  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Verifying Map Rendering**\n\nI\'m focusing on `InteractiveMapWidget.tsx`. I\'ve realized that whenever `selectedDay` or a tab changes, we need to ensure `map.invalidateSize()` is triggered with a small delay or on mount/update. This is key to ensuring Leaflet map tiles render fully within their bounds, preventing any visual clipping or sizing issues. I\'m now double-checking the code to ensure user experience is consistent across all states.\n\n\n**Addressing Dark Mode Issue**\n\nI\'ve tackled the dark mode issue. Initially, the app defaulted to dark mode due to the user\'s OS settings and how Tailwind compiles the `dark:` variant. The `Navbar` wasn\'t properly connected to the state, and `index.css` lacked the necessary `@custom-variant dark`. My solution was to add this variant in `index.css`, implement `isDarkMode` state in `App.tsx`, toggle the `dark` class on the `document.documentElement` based on this state, and pass the state and a toggle function to the `Navbar`. Clean styling has been ensured for both modes. I\'m now turning my attention to the non-functional pages tab.\n\n\n**Refactoring Tab Navigation**\n\nThe tab navigation in `ItineraryView.tsx` was misbehaving. The `TripSummaryHeader` and `Action Toolbar` remained static, confusing users when they clicked tabs. To fix this, I\'m repositioning the `TripSummaryHeader` and `Action Toolbar` as a banner at the top. I\'ll place tab content below it, to ensure an intuitive tab-switching experience. Specifically, the \"Day-by-Day Plan\" tab\'s layout now needs restructuring, to enhance clarity and flow, ensuring elements like `InteractiveMapWidget` render appropriately.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 2
      nanos: 426156882
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
